 {:name "exclude-the-real-unit-segment-from-a-principal-fourth-root-image"
  :lane :arc-lane
  :level :branch-sensitive-algebra
  :status :draft
  :body
  {:hook
   "If the principal fourth root were a real `q ∈ [0,1]`, raising it to the fourth power would force the source `η` to be real with `0 ≤ η.re ≤ 1`, contradicting the slit-plane invariant."
   :how-to-apply
   ["Assume `η^(1/4)` has zero imaginary part and real part `q` in `[0,1]`."
    "Use the principal-power identity `(η^(1/4))^4 = η` under the established nonzero/branch hypotheses."
    "Project the equality to real and imaginary parts."
    "Show `η.im = 0` and `η.re = q^4 ≤ 1`."
    "Contradict the incoming disjunction `1 < η.re ∨ η.im ≠ 0`."]
   :problem-class
   "Exclude a deleted real segment from the image of a branch-sensitive complex root when argument bounds alone only prove wedge membership."
