  {:hook
   "Evaluate the exponentially damped sinc integral as `arctan(1/a)`, then combine fixed-interval damping removal with a uniform Dirichlet tail bound to identify the undamped limit as `π/2`."
   :how-to-apply
   ["First prove convergence of the undamped positive-half-line integrals from the integration-by-parts tail estimate `|∫_A^B sinc| ≤ 2/A`."
    "Represent `sinc x` as `∫₀¹ cos(t*x) dt`."
    "For `a > 0`, prove product integrability and use Fubini to evaluate `∫₀∞ exp(-a*x)*sinc x dx` as `∫₀¹ a/(a²+t²) dt = arctan(1/a)`."
    "Apply Abel summation to the primitive of `sinc` and obtain a damped tail bound uniform in `a`, here `|∫_A^B exp(-a*x)*sinc x dx| ≤ 4/A`."
    "Pass the finite damped tail estimate to the improper tail."
    "On a fixed interval `[0,A]`, remove the damping by dominated convergence as `a → 0+`."
    "Use a three-error decomposition: undamped head near its limit, damped head near the undamped head, and uniformly small damped tail."
    "Compare the resulting damped limit with `arctan(1/a) → π/2` and use uniqueness of limits."
    "Use evenness of `Real.sinc` to double the positive-half-line limit and obtain the symmetric value `π`."]
   :problem-class
   "Evaluate a conditionally convergent improper oscillatory integral when Mathlib has neither the final sinc theorem nor a directly packaged Abel theorem."
